//    point, then CloseConstrainedSpan (cost 1) if a complete prefix exists,
//    then break. This is cheaper than CloseSpanWithinBudget(30) (which regressed
//    attempt 9) and still closes the span whenever any sub-expression was valid.
//
// 2. Per-span length guard (source of unterminated / ternary-expression traps):
//    The grammar may accept Python-style ternary `expr if cond else expr`,
//    causing "<<end_time - start_time + 24 if" patterns that never complete.
//    If |currentConstrainedOut| >= 30 tokens, call RollbackConstrainedToComplete
//    (cost 0) then CloseConstrainedSpan (cost 1) if complete, or
//    CloseSpanWithinBudget(1) (cost 1) as a forced fallback. The loop then
//    continues so subsequent spans can still be generated.
